  "steps": [
    "Heat 1 tbsp (15 ml) olive oil in a 5-quart Dutch oven over medium-high heat for 2 minutes until shimmering.",
    "Add 1 medium diced yellow onion (150 g) and 1 medium diced red bell pepper (150 g); cook over medium-high heat for 4 to 5 minutes, stirring occasionally, until onions are translucent and peppers are softened.",
    "Add 2 minced garlic cloves (6 g) and 1 lb (454 g) ground turkey; cook over medium-high heat for 5 to 6 minutes, breaking up the meat with a wooden spoon, until no pink remains and turkey reaches an internal temperature of 165°F (74°C).",
    "Stir in 2 tbsp (32 g) tomato paste, 1 tbsp (8 g) chili powder, 1 tsp (3 g) ground cumin, 1/2 tsp (1 g) smoked paprika, 1/2 tsp (1 g) dried oregano, 1/2 tsp (3 g) salt, and 1/4 tsp (1 g) black pepper; cook over medium heat for 1 minute until fragrant.",
    "Pour in one 14.5 oz (411 g) can diced tomatoes with juices, one 15 oz (250 g) can rinsed kidney beans, one 15 oz (250 g) can rinsed black beans, and 1 cup (240 ml) low-sodium chicken broth.",
    "Bring liquid to a boil over high heat, then reduce heat to medium-low and simmer uncovered for 8 to 10 minutes, stirring occasionally, until chili thickens and lightly coats the back of a spoon."
  ],
  "tips": [
    "Top each bowl with 2 tablespoons of non-fat plain Greek yogurt for an extra 3 grams of protein without added heavy fat.",
    "For a thicker consistency, mash half of the kidney beans with a fork before adding them to the pot.",
    "Double the recipe to split into four glass prep containers for high-protein lunches during the week."
  ],
  "storage": "Store in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 4 days, or freeze in freezer-safe containers for up to 3 months.",
